    "justification": "Finite rational protocol weights and finite branch coverage make the operational optimum attained and auditable.",
    "gap": "Fixed-source identification alone neither prices protocols nor returns sparse physical ownership records.",
    "consumer": "Counterfactual bandit designers can inspect the exact minimum-cost acquisition and every branch transcript.",
    "proof_tex": "Operational feasibility means that some finite correctly typed acquired collection makes the specified complete run accept.  Theorem \\(\\mathrm{Switching\\ source\\ normal\\ form}\\) converts it to an accepted switching certificate without increasing cost.  Therefore the cover family in Theorem \\(\\mathrm{Switching\\ weighted\\mbox{-}cover\\ frontier}\\) is nonempty.  There are at most \\(2^{|\\mathcal A|}\\) protocols and all weights are finite nonnegative binary rationals, so the finite minimum\n\\[\n W^*=\\min_{\\mathcal P\\subseteq\\Pi:\\,cup_{S\\in\\mathcal P}K_{\\mathrm{sw}}(S)=\\Omega}\n \\sum_{S\\in\\mathcal P}w(S)\n\\tag{1}\n\\]\nis attained.  The cover identity gives \\(W^*=\\operatorname{Opt}_{\\mathrm{sw}}\\).\n\nFor each branch, choose a successful witness from an optimal cover and split ownership into singleton records.  The normal-form proof verifies all record-local clauses and the full-run clause, so the resulting certificate is accepted and has cost \\(W^*\\).  The family of its canonical sparse encodings is finite: there are \\(M\\) branch indices; every protocol, label, and source mask has fixed finite width; and Lemma \\(\\mathrm{Fixed\\ transcript\\ size}\\) bounds each transcript.  Thus a lexicographically first minimum-cost member exists.  By definition it is \\(E_{\\mathrm{sw}}^{\\star}\\).  The canonical certificate bound gives\n\\[\n N_{E_{\\mathrm{sw}}^{\\star}}\\le B_{\\mathrm{sw}}.\n\\tag{2}\n\\]\nThe weighted-cover theorem's self-reduction returns this member and proves that each singleton owner needs only \\(\\lceil\\log_2(M+1)\\rceil\\) bits.  Its decoded fields are exactly the protocol, label, source, branch-index, and transcript outputs listed in the claim.\n\nDuring incidence construction and self-reduction, cache the response under the \\(|\\mathcal A|\\)-bit protocol mask.  Therefore a distinct protocol is queried at most once.  Definition \\(\\mathrm{Certificate\\mbox{-}independent\\ physical\\ input}\\) places every query and response bit in \\(N_{\\mathcal O}\\).  Positivity is checked only for the event in each actually considered source slice, as equation (2) of the normal-form proof shows.  Nothing in (1)--(2) identifies a numerical value of \\(Q\\), and every appeal to CTFIDU\\({}^{+}\\) is to the operational acceptance test, which proves the final qualification.",
